## Installation and local run

Because this is a static front-end demo, there is no dependency installation step.

Open the file directly in a browser:

```bash
open index.html
```

Or serve it locally:

```bash
python3 -m http.server 8000
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:8000
```

## Environment variables

There are no application environment variables configured in this codebase.

This is important: the app does not currently use a real backend or secret-bearing configuration, so there are no production credentials to expose.

## Supabase configuration

No Supabase schema, migrations, security policies, connection code, or service-role keys are present in the repository state available here.

The app currently uses in-browser localStorage instead of Supabase. That means:

- no production authentication
- no secure profile ownership model
- no RLS enforcement
- no database-backed record persistence
- no real opportunity application processing

